# .gitignore
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECURITY NOTE: Any file you intend to keep out of version control must be
# listed here AND removed from git tracking if previously committed.
#
# To purge already-committed files that should be ignored:
#   git rm --cached <file>          (single file)
#   git rm --cached -r <directory>  (directory)
#   git commit -m "chore: remove tracked files now in .gitignore"
#
# IMMEDIATE ACTIONS REQUIRED after pulling this file:
#
#   FIX #10 — desktop.ini files (Windows folder metadata, leaked dev OS):
#     git rm --cached $(git ls-files "**/desktop.ini" "desktop.ini") 2>/dev/null
#     git commit -m "chore: remove tracked desktop.ini artifacts"
#
#   FIX #9 — metadata.json (AI tooling fingerprint, Gemini API capability disclosure):
#     git rm --cached metadata.json 2>/dev/null
#     git commit -m "chore: remove metadata.json AI build artifact"
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Next.js build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
out/
build/
dist/

# ── Environment files — NEVER commit secrets ──────────────────────────────────
.env*
!.env.example

# ── Testing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# ── Misc ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ── Sentry ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.sentryclirc

# ── Visual Studio ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vs/

# ── Windows artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FIX #10: desktop.ini files are Windows folder metadata that reveal the dev
# environment (Windows machine) and contain no useful project information.
# The file in /public/ was publicly served at /desktop.ini — now blocked.
# Run the git rm command above to remove already-committed files from tracking.
desktop.ini
**/desktop.ini
Thumbs.db

# ── AI build artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FIX #9: metadata.json is a Gemini AI Studio build artifact accidentally
# committed to the repo. It exposes MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API,
# fingerprinting the codebase as AI-generated and revealing AI tooling details.
# Run: git rm --cached metadata.json && git commit -m "chore: remove metadata.json"
metadata.json

# ── Cryptographic keys — NEVER commit ────────────────────────────────────────
# Private PGP / GPG keys must NEVER be placed in /public or committed to git.
# The PUBLIC key (/public/pgp-key.txt) is safe to commit.
# The PRIVATE key must be stored in a password manager or secrets vault.
public/PRIVATE-KEY-KEEP-SECRET*
public/PRIVATE-KEY*
public/*private*
*.private.key
*.secret.key
